- Eliminated lines with zero execution counts.
- Added line counters to ensure that line numbers remain contiguous irrespective of skipped lines in the printed output (-.c.gcda).

Building : 

- Install Pre-requisites : ./contrib/download_prerequisites (*run inside the Top Level Directory (gcc) ).

Builds in the top level directory are not allowed. Create a separate build directory outside the Top Level Directory for the build itself.

(*must not run this command inside the gcov tld itself, must be run in the same parent directory that contains gcov, ex. Desktop etc.)

- mkdir gcc-build 
    cd gcc-build

(*To run inside the build directory - gcc-build .)

- ../gcc/configure --prefix=$HOME/gcc-install --disable-multilib --enable-languages=c,c++
    make -j$(nproc)
    make install

Notes :

- gcc requires flex and bison to generate its lexer during the build, to avoid running into errors ensure both have been installed before building : 

    apt install flex
    apt install bison

- LIBRARY_PATH must not contain a trailing colon or a reference to the current directory.

Running and Testing :

Once the build has completed, gcov can be invoked on a test file (ex. test.c) by running : 

~/gcc-install/bin/gcc --coverage test.c -o test
    ./test
    ~/gcc-install/bin/gcov test.c
    
- The output can be viewed using : 
    cat test.c.gcov

The Annotated code should not contain lines that were not executed, such lines would be prefixed with a "####" in an ordinary gcc build in the test.c.gcda . 
